{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Localization of a Module.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Localization of a Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"localization of a module localization of a module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Localization of a Module.md","fileName":"Localization of a Module.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Localization of a Module","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 20:00\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Projective Flat and Injective Modules]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Projective Flat and Injective Modules","Scalar Extension for Modules","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Localization of a Module.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Localization of a Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"localization of a module localization of a module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Localization of a Module.md","fileName":"Localization of a Module.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Localization of a Module","heading":"Localization of a Module","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The localization S⁻¹M of an R-module M consists of fractions m/s with s in a multiplicatively closed set. It is naturally a module over the localized ring S⁻¹R.\n\nThere is a canonical isomorphism S⁻¹M ≅ S⁻¹R ⊗_R M. This identifies module localization as [[Scalar Extension for Modules]] and explains its exactness.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Projective Flat and Injective Modules","Scalar Extension for Modules","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Localization of a Module.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Localization of a Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"localization of a module localization of a module","fi